course: dictionary
lesson: 6330
title: Mottos and what they stand for
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A motto is a short sentence or phrase that sums up what a person, school, family or country believes in or aims to do. Context helps you here too. «My motto is: always be kind.» The words after "my motto is" tell you the motto is a sentence about how someone lives.
explain: Many schools have a motto, often printed on the badge, and some are in Latin. Families and countries can have mottos too. «The suffragettes' motto was Deeds not words.» The motto is short, and it tells you the group wanted action, not just talk.
explain: A motto is not a long story. It is a few words that stand for big ideas. «Live for others!» is only four words, but it describes a whole way of living.
fact: A motto is a short sentence or phrase.
fact: A motto sums up the beliefs or aims of a person, school, family or country.
fact: «Deeds not words» was the motto of the suffragettes.
fact: «Satyameva jayate» means "Truth alone triumphs", and it is now India's national motto.
fact: The Salvation Army's motto of care is often put as soup, soap and salvation.
exercise: What does a motto sum up? | the number of pupils in a class | the length of a book | *the beliefs or aims of a person, school, family or country | the weather for the week
exercise: «Satyameva jayate» means "Truth alone triumphs." What does this motto suggest? | that you should never speak | *that truth wins in the end | that lies always win | that school starts at nine
exercise: Mia says, «Always be kind» is her motto. What does this tell you about Mia? | She dislikes her family | *Kindness matters to her and guides how she lives | She has never been to school | She is always cold
test: Where is a school motto often found? | *on the school badge | in the bus timetable | in the school lunch menu | under the playground
test: What three words make up the Salvation Army's motto of care, as often put? | cup, cake and candy | sun, sea and sand | hat, hope and happiness | *soup, soap and salvation
exam: Which of these is the best example of a motto? | Dogs like long walks in the park | The bus leaves at eight | It rained all week | *Live for others!
